# Plain `vp dev` reads `.env`, but it does not provide Cloudflare Durable
# Object, Queue, Workflow, or asset bindings. GitHub OAuth, Monkeytype,
# community mutations, firmware builds, and extension pairing require:
#
#   vp run dev:worker
#
# Keep Worker configuration in the gitignored `.dev.vars`, using
# `.dev.vars.example` as the source of truth. Do not copy local values into
# production.
#
# Origins:
#   local BETTER_AUTH_URL      = http://127.0.0.1:8787
#   production BETTER_AUTH_URL = https://kbui.jonfonts.workers.dev
#
# Production GitHub URLs:
#   OAuth App homepage         = https://kbui.jonfonts.workers.dev
#   OAuth App callback         = https://kbui.jonfonts.workers.dev/api/auth/callback/github
#   GitHub App homepage        = https://kbui.jonfonts.workers.dev
#   GitHub App callback        = https://kbui.jonfonts.workers.dev/api/auth/firmware/github/callback
#   GitHub App setup URL       = https://kbui.jonfonts.workers.dev/api/auth/firmware/github/setup
#   GitHub App webhook URL     = https://kbui.jonfonts.workers.dev/api/webhooks/github
#
# Required Worker runtime names (13):
#   BETTER_AUTH_SECRET
#   BETTER_AUTH_URL
#   GITHUB_CLIENT_ID
#   GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET
#   MONKEYTYPE_SECRET_KEY
#   GITHUB_APP_SLUG
#   GITHUB_APP_ID
#   GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_ID
#   GITHUB_APP_CLIENT_SECRET
#   GITHUB_APP_INSTALL_URL
#   GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY
#   GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET
#   GITHUB_APP_TOKEN_SECRET_KEY
#
# GitHub Actions reserves secret names beginning with GITHUB_. Repository
# secrets therefore use GH_CLIENT_ID, GH_CLIENT_SECRET, GH_APP_SLUG, GH_APP_ID,
# GH_APP_CLIENT_ID, GH_APP_CLIENT_SECRET, GH_APP_INSTALL_URL,
# GH_APP_PRIVATE_KEY, GH_WEBHOOK_SECRET, and GH_APP_TOKEN_SECRET_KEY. The deploy
# workflow maps those aliases back to the GITHUB_* Worker runtime names.
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, BETTER_AUTH_URL, and MONKEYTYPE_SECRET_KEY keep their names.
#
# Optional runtime rate-limit tokens are documented in `.dev.vars.example`.
# Local GitHub webhook tunneling is available with:
#
#   vp run dev:webhook
